note.p:
In the omitted portion of Part B, four major potential political roles for the General Assembly were listed, as follows:
“(a) To substitute for the moribund Security Council as the UN action body in the event of breaches of the peace and acts of aggression, such as another Korea;
“(b) To work out the peaceful settlement of political disputes, both East-West issues (Germany, Austria, Trieste, etc.) and other political questions (Palestine, KMT troops in Burma, etc.);
“(c) To ease the tensions and strains in the complex of changing colonial relationships, and
“(d) To serve as a forum and sounding board for both sides in the cold war.”
